diff --git a/changelog.d/cli-v-prefix.feature.rst b/changelog.d/cli-v-prefix.feature.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..014e24c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/cli-v-prefix.feature.rst
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+The ``pysemver`` subcommands now accept an optional leading ``v`` or ``V`` on version arguments (for example git tags like ``v1.4.2``). Output is printed without the prefix.
diff --git a/changelog.d/compare-dict.deprecation.rst b/changelog.d/compare-dict.deprecation.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dc6bc06
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/compare-dict.deprecation.rst
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Passing a :class:`dict` to :meth:`semver.version.Version.compare` is deprecated and now emits a :class:`DeprecationWarning`. Strings, tuples, lists and :class:`~semver.version.Version` instances are still accepted.
diff --git a/changelog.d/next-version-token.deprecation.rst b/changelog.d/next-version-token.deprecation.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9030c1a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/next-version-token.deprecation.rst
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+The ``prerelease_token`` keyword of :meth:`semver.version.Version.next_version` is deprecated in favour of ``token``, matching :meth:`~semver.version.Version.bump_prerelease` and :meth:`~semver.version.Version.bump_build`. The old keyword still works and does not emit a warning.
